snapctrlalt (1.3.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The overlay now re-checks the image-to-canvas scale against the measured
    window size when it opens.  A first launch (autostart, or right after login
    before X is settled) can fail to read the root window and fall back to the
    wrong scale, which showed up as the whole capture being offset; the ratio is
    now corrected automatically and the change is logged.
  * The settings window gained a "toolbar presentation" dropdown (overlay or
    editor window), equivalent to Ctrl+E, and an explicit debug switch for the
    mask variant, which is known not to work.
  * Documented all three toolbar presentations in the README, including why the
    mask variant is disabled and the exact configuration needed to re-enable it
    for debugging.

