snapctrlalt (1.3.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The toolbar in the editor window was smaller than the one in the overlay:
    its width was tied to the capture width, so a 936 px capture squeezed the
    UI scale down to 1.54.  The toolbar size now depends only on the UI scale
    (1204x152 for every capture size); a narrow window scrolls it instead of
    shrinking it.
  * Removed the draggable-toolbar experiment added in 1.3.3.  It was my own
    stand-in for the "toolbar on the mask" request, was not asked for, and
    changed the default behaviour; the toolbar follows the selection again.
  * toolbar_mode: mask (a separate window floating over the mask) is now
    disabled outright and falls back to canvas with a log line, instead of
    staying selectable while not working.

